  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-05-04T21:36:36.421Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "With the recent updates to VRChat, any object that would use a method of freezing objects relative to world space would cause the objects to jitter or freak out when moving armature or any part of the body that's activated via animation. The network currently has synced up normal constrained objects with users' IK. Everything else just stutters when users are moving and can cause desync on remote instances as well as local instances in given circumstances. This is something that should be looked into especially since the new Avatar Dynamics system stutters a lot with Senders and Receivers tied with world constrained objects",
